8 news now i-team has been investigating  problems inside prisons vanessa murphy  here with more of some of the key points  from this department of corrections  audit that the i-team obtained vanessa  denise and brian the audit points out  many claims about use of force inside  prisons are not being investigated this  could be an inmate reporting a claim  against an officer or vice versa several  different scenarios fit into that  category the audit also points to a lack  of training with firearms tasers even a  restraint chair and a 25 percent job  vacancy rate and the audit states use of  force data collected by the department  is inaccurate incomplete and unreliable  the audit says the department needs to  shape up to ensure prisons are safe and  humane it came up with 16  recommendations and provided examples  like out of a sample of 20 reports  alleging excessive use of force there  was no evidence the inspector general's  office even looked at them and after an  officer fired a blank round from a  shotgun during a use of force incident  there was no evidence he had up-to-date  training in a letter the n-d-o-c  director stated changes would be made in  response to that legislative council  bureau's audit when i interviewed  governor steve sisilak in january i  brought up issues about this lack of  transparency do you think the doc needs  to be more transparent and are you doing  anything about it well we try to be as  transparent as we possibly can i would  encourage all of my departments to be as  transparent as we can they're subject to  the same rules and regulations that all  state agencies are and the public has a  right to know what's going on because  someone's incarcerated doesn't take away  all their rights  a prison spokesman did reach out to me  after that interview with the governor  we are still working to get information  about various issues though and just  today the department denied one of our  requests we have more information about  that audit at 8newsnow.com from the  i-team's david charns
 

